Subject: [PATCH] Point Bolt URLs at boltapp.com (plugin 2.9.0)

Port of the bolt-magento2 domain migration (BoltApp/bolt-magento2 #1973) onto
the Magento 1 plugin's 2.9.0 release tag, extended to every bolt.com reference
in the tree.

Runtime hosts: the six constants in Helper/UrlTrait.php -- api, connect and
merchant, production and sandbox -- move from bolt.com to boltapp.com.
Block/Checkout/Boltpay.php builds connect.js and track.js from them, and the
API, GraphQL and configuration helpers go through getApiUrl() and
getBoltMerchantUrl(), so that is the whole request surface. The admin help
text in etc/system.xml that names merchant.bolt.com/settings moves with them.

Apple Pay placeholder: Block/Checkout/Boltpay.php compares the prefilled
email against na@bolt.com to detect Apple Pay's masked address. Bolt's
checkout still sends na@bolt.com today, so the check now accepts both
na@bolt.com and na@boltapp.com instead of swapping one for the other.

Help links: docs.bolt.com and support.bolt.com no longer resolve, and no
Magento 1 page exists on help.boltapp.com, so the installation and
operations links in README.md, refund_popup.phtml and update_popup.phtml
point at the help centre root, and the production-readiness article at
help.boltapp.com/developers/production-readiness-guides/.

Metadata: the copyright header in every file (2.9.0 ships 106 of them,
tests included) reads https://www.boltapp.com; composer.json's homepage
and dev@ contact address move to boltapp.com.

Left alone: dummy test fixtures such as test@bolt.com and https://bolt.com
image URLs, the *.dev.bolt.me and *-staging.bolt.com custom-URL test cases,
and CHANGELOG.md, which has no bolt.com reference.

Apply from the Magento root (the directory that holds app/ and js/):

    git apply bolt-magento1-2.9.0-boltapp-domains.patch
    # or, without git:
    patch -p1 < bolt-magento1-2.9.0-boltapp-domains.patch

---
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@
 5.4+
 
 ## Installation guide
-[Magento 1 plugin installation guide](https://docs.bolt.com/docs/magento-1-integration)
+[Magento 1 plugin installation guide](https://help.boltapp.com/)
 
 ## Run tests
 
